1. Executive Summary

This document outlines a comprehensive and deeply technical direction to migrate legacy MuleSoft APIs built using RAML to OpenAPI Specification (OAS) 3.0. The migration architecture emphasizes automated conversion, modular flows, CI/CD enablement, and testing strategies such as Consumer Driven Contract Testing (CDCT) using Pact, functional testing using Karate, and test plan management with qTest.

2. Objectives

Establish OpenAPI 3.0 as the standard for all API definitions

Provide modular automation pipelines for RAML-to-OAS transformation

Enable CDCT using Pact, to allow service providers to release independently

Integrate Karate for advanced API functional and regression testing

Manage test plans, traceability, and execution reporting using qTest

3. Scope

Partial automation of RAML-to-OAS conversion

Cloud-hosted conversion pipeline using AWS Lambda

Integration with GitHub-based API repositories

Refactor API implementations using APIKit compatible with OAS 3.0

Build contract testing with Pact and functional validation using Karate

Seamlessly manage test lifecycle with qTest

4. Migration Architecture Overview

Architecture Pillars:

Source Repositories: GitHub (RAML & OAS)

Conversion Layer: AWS Lambda + RamlToOpenApiConverter (NuGet)

API Implementation: MuleSoft APIKit (OAS-compatible)

Test Strategies: Pact (contract), Karate (functional), qTest (traceability)

Developer Experience: Spec linters, CI/CD, semantic versioning

5. Detailed Migration Steps

Step 1: API Inventory and Categorization

Catalog all RAML APIs from GitHub repositories

Tag metadata: domain, consumer count, owning team, change cadence

Define migration waves prioritizing high-use and core data APIs

Step 2: RAML-to-OAS Conversion Using Lambda

Flow Diagram:

+-------------------+        +--------------+         +----------------------------+
| GitHub (RAML API) | ---->  | Webhook Event| ----->  | AWS Lambda Conversion Job |
+-------------------+        +--------------+         +----------------------------+
                                                         |
                                                         v
                                     +------------------------------------------+
                                     | Store converted OAS in GitHub branch     |
                                     +------------------------------------------+

Technical Details:

NuGet package: RamlToOpenApiConverter

Lambda function runs Python or .NET core handler

Output conforms to OAS 3.0 with tags, descriptions, securitySchemes

Additional script validates result via Spectral Linter

Step 3: MuleSoft Refactor with APIKit for OAS

Flow Diagram:

+----------------------------+        +---------------------------+
| GitHub (OAS Spec Branch)  | -----> | MuleSoft Anypoint Studio  |
+----------------------------+        +---------------------------+
                                                |
                                                v
                               +-----------------------------------------+
                               | Use APIKit OAS router to auto-generate |
                               | flow scaffolds                          |
                               +-----------------------------------------+
                                                |
                                                v
                                     +--------------------------+
                                     | Deploy to Sandbox Env     |
                                     +--------------------------+

Implementation Details:

APIKit generates scaffold using oas-router

Backward compatibility built into flows

Supports versioning headers or path-based routing

Step 4: Consumer Driven Contract Testing with Pact

Flow Diagram:

+----------------------+         +----------------------+
| Consumer Pact Tests  | ----->  | Pact Broker          |
| (defined in DSL)     |         | (versioned contracts) |
+----------------------+         +----------------------+
                                          |
                                          v
+--------------------------+     +----------------------------+
| MuleSoft CI Pipeline     | <-- | Provider Verification Tool |
+--------------------------+     +----------------------------+

Implementation Notes:

Pact contracts are versioned and fetched dynamically from Pact Broker

Provider verification runs during CI

Broken contracts fail early and point to affected interactions

Sample Pact Contract (Consumer DSL)

{
  "consumer": { "name": "AppX" },
  "provider": { "name": "CustomerService" },
  "interactions": [
    {
      "description": "Get user by ID",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/users/42"
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": 42,
          "name": "Alice"
        },
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

Step 5: Functional and Regression Testing with Karate

Flow Diagram:

+--------------------+    +--------------------+    +-------------------------+
| Karate Feature     | -> | Karate CLI / Maven | -> | JUnit XML Reports       |
| Scripts (BDD Gherkin)|  +--------------------+    +-------------------------+
                                                             |
                                                             v
                                                 +-------------------------+
                                                 | Upload to qTest         |
                                                 +-------------------------+

Example Karate Test:

Feature: Retrieve Customer Info

  Scenario: Get customer 123
    Given url 'https://api.mydomain.com/customers/123'
    When method GET
    Then status 200
    And match response contains { id: 123, name: 'Alice' }

Step 7: qTest Integration for Reporting and Traceability

qTest Integration Flow:

+-------------------------+      +-------------------+
| Test Automation Output | ---> | qTest API Adapter |
+-------------------------+      +-------------------+
                                       |
                                       v
                          +-----------------------------+
                          | Test Run + Result Dashboard |
                          +-----------------------------+

CI pipeline invokes script: upload-results-to-qtest.sh

Maps JUnit test cases to qTest Test Runs

Enables traceability from API Spec → Test → Release

6. Governance and Versioning

Use Semantic Versioning (e.g., v1.2.0) per API

Validate specs using Spectral (naming, status codes, tags)

Contracts are immutable once verified

Update changelogs and API portals with each deployment

